{"name":"Husk","hex":"#b2994b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Husk","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Husk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Husk","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a husk is the outer shell or coating of a seed. In the United States, the term husk often refers to the leafy outer covering of an ear of maize (corn) as it grows on the plant. Literally, a husk or hull includes the protective outer covering of a seed, fruit, or vegetable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Involucre_d%27un_noisetier_de_Bysance.jpg/330px-Involucre_d%27un_noisetier_de_Bysance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husk","wikidata":"Q14524280"},{"title":"Husk (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Husk is a superhero appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. First appearing in Rom Annual #3 as the younger sister of X-Men member Cannonball, she was created by Bill Mantlo and William Johnson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/35/Uncannyxmen432.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husk_(comics)","wikidata":"Q2714915"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/E8025-Milyanfan-corn-huskers.jpg/500px-E8025-Milyanfan-corn-huskers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/E8025-Milyanfan-corn-huskers.jpg/1280px-E8025-Milyanfan-corn-huskers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/E8025-Milyanfan-corn-huskers.jpg/500px-E8025-Milyanfan-corn-huskers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Corn being husked in the yard of a Dungan farmer in Kyrgyzstan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AE8025-Milyanfan-corn-huskers.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Africa_Food_Security_11_%2810665081134%29.jpg/500px-Africa_Food_Security_11_%2810665081134%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Africa_Food_Security_11_%2810665081134%29.jpg/1280px-Africa_Food_Security_11_%2810665081134%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Africa_Food_Security_11_%2810665081134%29.jpg/500px-Africa_Food_Security_11_%2810665081134%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A woman manually dehusking corn in Malawi. People working in subsistence agricultural settings tend not to have the mechanization of processing practices to reduce the labor. In many societies, this labor falls to family members such as women, who make up the majority of farmers working in smallholdings.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAfrica_Food_Security_11_(10665081134).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/af/Xmen_AOApokalipse_FinalVersion_by_martegodpopo.jpg/120px-Xmen_AOApokalipse_FinalVersion_by_martegodpopo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/af/Xmen_AOApokalipse_FinalVersion_by_martegodpopo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/af/Xmen_AOApokalipse_FinalVersion_by_martegodpopo.jpg/120px-Xmen_AOApokalipse_FinalVersion_by_martegodpopo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paige's AoA look","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AXmen_AOApokalipse_FinalVersion_by_marte